---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import {
  ADSENSE_CMP_CONFIGURED,
  ADSENSE_CONFIGURED,
  CONTACT_EMAIL,
} from '../data/site-config';

const privacyDescription =
  'What happens to the files you process on Kit-Bin, what data is and isn\'t collected, and how Adsterra advertising and consent choices work.';
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | Kit-Bin"
  description={privacyDescription}
>
  <div class="max-w-2xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 space-y-6 text-ink dark:text-slate-300">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold text-ink dark:text-slate-100">Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="text-sm text-muted dark:text-slate-500">Last updated: August 2026</p>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Your files</h2>
      <p>
        Every tool on this site currently processes files entirely in your browser, using
        WebAssembly and native browser APIs. Your file is read into your browser's memory, the
        conversion runs on your device, and the result downloads directly to your device. At no
        point is a file you select uploaded to any server. This applies to every tool currently
        live on the site. None of them use a server fallback. If that changes for a specific
        tool in the future (for very large files or a format that genuinely can't be processed
        client-side), that tool's own page will say so explicitly.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Accounts and storage</h2>
      <p>
        There are no user accounts on this site. Files you select or process are not uploaded to
        or stored on Kit-Bin servers, and Kit-Bin does not maintain a database of user files.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Analytics</h2>
      <p>
        This site does not currently run any analytics or tracking script. If aggregate,
        cookieless usage analytics (page views, general device/location category, not
        individual tracking) are added in the future, this section will be updated to say so
        before that happens.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="advertising">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Advertising</h2>
      <p>
        Kit-Bin shows a small number of standard banner advertisements, served by Adsterra, to help
        cover hosting and development costs. These are static banner ads, not video, not audio, and
        not a full-screen interstitial. They never appear inside a file drop area or in a way that
        could be mistaken for part of a tool.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Your download is never gated behind an advertisement. The moment a tool finishes processing,
        the download is available, whatever your cookie choice. If you have accepted advertising
        cookies, a banner may appear alongside the progress indicator while the file is genuinely
        being processed, and it disappears as soon as the file is ready. It never delays the file
        and never sits between you and the download button.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Adsterra's advertising resources are not requested at all until you accept the cookie banner
        shown on your first visit. If you decline, or before you choose either way, no advertising
        script or advertising cookie loads, and every tool continues to work exactly the same either
        way. You can change your choice at any time using{' '}
        <strong>Privacy and cookie settings</strong> in the footer, which also removes any advertising
        already loaded on the page.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        Once loaded, Adsterra and its advertising partners may use cookies, pixels, or similar
        technologies for ad delivery, measurement, and fraud prevention, and where permitted,
        limited personalization. This is entirely separate from how your files are handled: the
        advertising code runs in an isolated frame and is never given a file's name, contents, or any
        conversion setting. Kit-Bin does not pass any of that information to Adsterra, intentionally
        or otherwise, because the advertising component has no access to the file-processing code at
        all.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        {ADSENSE_CONFIGURED ? (
          <>
            Kit-Bin also uses Google AdSense. Google may process information such as the page URL, IP
            address, browser information, and advertising identifiers to serve, measure, and protect
            advertising. See{' '}
            <a href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/partner-sites" class="underline">
              how Google uses information from sites that use its services
            </a>. {ADSENSE_CMP_CONFIGURED
              ? 'Privacy and cookie choices for AdSense are presented through the configured Google CMP.'
              : 'AdSense is configured but its Google CMP is not yet enabled, so personalized AdSense advertising is not served to UK, EEA, or Swiss visitors until that is in place.'}
          </>
        ) : (
          'Google AdSense is not active on Kit-Bin yet. This section will be updated with the details above before AdSense is enabled.'
        )}
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-ink dark:text-slate-100 mb-2">Contact</h2>
      <p>
        Questions about this policy: <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`} class="underline">{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a>
      </p>
    </section>
  </div>
</Layout>
